  "description": "Major Programme Requirement Studies in Fine Arts are divided into THREE main streams: (1) Art History – studies the historical development of art with a special emphasis on China; (2) Studio Art – trains students in the practice of artistic creation; and (3) Art History and Studio Art – applies equal emphasis on both. Students must declare one of the streams at the beginning of their third year of attendance. Students are required to complete a minimum of 72 units of courses as follows:",
